// A mirror's prefix is the start of a C identifier, its `enum:` an enumeration or an integer type
// written as C writes one, and it has one `@c`.
// error: `prefix:` is the start of the enumerators' names, and `1E_` is not the start of a C identifier
// error: `enum:` names the C enum the type mirrors, and `int *` is not an enumeration or an integer type
// error: `enum:` names the C enum the type mirrors, and `e_t (` is not a C type: `(` is not part of a C type
// error: a C enum mirror has one `@c`

@c(enum: "e_t", prefix: "1E_")
data BadPrefix
  One

@c(enum: "int *", prefix: "E_")
data Pointer
  One

@c(enum: "e_t (", prefix: "E_")
data Unreadable
  One

@c(enum: "e_t")
@c(enum: "f_t")
data TwoAnnotations
  One

main() = 0
